## 2. the demo's commit messages
$ git log -1 --format='%s%n%n%b' <E10 line 42's tip> | sed -n '1,12p'
<bench> image v8: the AX200 keeps its firmware BAR, and soundserver dumps the ALC287's COEFs and GPIO and runs Linux's ALC287 COEF init

Measurement-only; never lands.

Wi-Fi. v7's laptop boot handed 8086:2723 over, then pcidev moved its BAR 0 to
0x450200000 and seven later 2 MiB windows; the bridge in front of it (00:02.2)
forwards only 0xd0600000..0xd0700000, so every moved BAR read 0xffffffff
and the claim was refused, netstack never got the card, and `wifi scan`
said "no netstack to ask". For 8086:2723 alone, place_bar now keeps the BAR
where firmware put it (0xd0600000, 2 MiB aligned, inside that window),
checks it against every other function's BARs and cut windows, records it
as cut, and logs "kept at ... where firmware put it" with the dword it
exit 0
